# CR 707.8a: a token created as a copy of a double-faced permanent is double-faced - but a Clone that copied one is no
# double-faced permanent (CR 707.8a's Clone example, 712.9), so a token copy of the Clone has one face, Outland Liberator's.
# Made at night, it has daybound yet is not represented by a double-faced card or token, so it neither enters transformed
# (CR 702.145b) nor transforms (CR 701.27c): it stays a front-face-up Outland Liberator, as the Clone does.
#
# Turn 1: Forest and Mox Emerald cast Outland Liberator (it becomes day, CR 702.145d); Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire cast
# Clone, copying it. Bot2 casts nothing on turn 2, so turn 3 is night (CR 731.2) and the Liberator becomes Frenzied
# Trapbreaker. Turn 3: Island, then Three Steps Ahead ({U} plus {3} for its token mode) on the Clone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Outland Liberator
Clone
Island
Three Steps Ahead
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
